        "title": "Why Economists Got Excited About a Tax Reform",
        "description": "Before GST, every time a part changed hands between businesses it was taxed again, tax on tax, all the way through the supply chain. This short explains how that quietly pushed firms to make their own parts badly rather than buy better ones from a specialist, and why GST's real win wasn't collecting more revenue, it was letting businesses build things the way that actually made sense.",
